# Context for src/Pos.Web/Dockerfile.
#
# node_modules is the one that matters most: pnpm's store is symlink-heavy and
# platform-specific, so a copy from a Windows host both defeats the cached
# install layer above the COPY and can produce a build with native binaries
# that cannot run on Linux.

node_modules/
dist/

## Test output and caches — none of it is part of a build
playwright-report/
blob-report/
test-results/
playwright/.cache/
coverage/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

## e2e/ is deliberately NOT excluded. `pnpm build` runs `tsc -b`, which builds every
## project in the solution — including tsconfig.e2e.json, whose playwright.config.ts
## imports ./e2e/fixtures/seed. Excluding it makes the image type-check *less* than CI
## does and fails the build with TS2307. None of it reaches the final image: the
## runtime stage copies dist/ and nothing else.

## Local environment overrides. .env.example carries no values and is harmless,
## but nothing in this directory should ever reach an image: Vite inlines VITE_*
## into the bundle, so a real value here would be published to every browser.
.env
.env.*

## Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
